.TH DIALOG 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
Dialog \- A speech box at the bottom of the screen that types its text out character by character and waits for the player to dismiss it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqdialog.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct Dialog {
  const char *speaker;
  const char *text;
  float chars_shown;
  float chars_per_sec;    /* 0 = 40 */
  bool  active;
  Font  font;             /* zero = debug font */
} Dialog;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A speech box at the bottom of the screen that types its text out character by character and waits for the player to dismiss it. One Dialog shows one line; a conversation is a sequence of dialog_show() calls driven by dialog_done(), or a cutscene of CUT_SAY steps. Keep one in a scene static (it holds pointers). Set font and chars_per_sec once; dialog_show() fills the rest.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B speaker
name drawn in yellow above the text, or NULL for none
.TP
.B text
the line; must stay valid while active (a string literal or static buffer)
.TP
.B chars_shown
how many characters have been revealed so far (fractional)
.TP
.B chars_per_sec
typing speed; 0 = 40
.TP
.B active
true from dialog_show() until the player dismisses the completed line
.TP
.B font
font for both speaker and text; a zero Font is the debug font
.SH MODULE
dialog (src/engine/dialog/dialog.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dialog_show (3),
.BR dialog_update (3),
.BR dialog_render (3),
.BR dialog_done (3),
.BR gge\-dialog (7),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
